From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stat: plain time lines when output is plain

Repository: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch
Base: fastfetch 2.70.0, 17bb3fd2384bd814b421d73b8c8b8d08e06cfa26
Problem: --stat writes each module's time with cursor movement and colour
sequences even with --pipe or redirected output, so a file got escape
sequences.
Solution: in pipe mode print the time as a line of its own after the
module's output, without any sequence.
Scope: common/impl/commandoption.c and common/impl/jsonconfig.c; terminal
output is unchanged.
Upstream-Status: suitable for upstream.
Verification: redirected --stat on pool v1-1, v11-1 and rpi-1 (2026-10-27)
contains no ESC byte.
Removal: when upstream keeps --stat output plain in pipe mode.
---
 src/common/impl/commandoption.c | 8 +++++++-
 src/common/impl/jsonconfig.c    | 8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/impl/commandoption.c b/src/common/impl/commandoption.c
index bc5ee9e..ae6c11d 100644
--- a/src/common/impl/commandoption.c
+++ b/src/common/impl/commandoption.c
@@ -303,7 +303,13 @@ void ffPrintCommandOption(FFdata* data) {
                                                                                                                      : FF_COLOR_FG_RED),
                         ms);
                 }
-                printf("\e7\e[1A\e[9999999C\e[%dD%s\e8", len - 1, str); // Save; Up 1; Right 9999999; Left <len - 1>; Print <str>; Load
+                if (instance.config.display.pipe) {
+                    // Plain output has no cursor control: the time goes on
+                    // a line of its own after the module's.
+                    printf("%.3fms\n", ms);
+                } else {
+                    printf("\e7\e[1A\e[9999999C\e[%dD%s\e8", len - 1, str); // Save; Up 1; Right 9999999; Left <len - 1>; Print <str>; Load
+                }
             }
         }
 
diff --git a/src/common/impl/jsonconfig.c b/src/common/impl/jsonconfig.c
index c0b14e2..6ec8f26 100644
--- a/src/common/impl/jsonconfig.c
+++ b/src/common/impl/jsonconfig.c
@@ -416,7 +416,13 @@ static const char* printJsonConfig(FFdata* data, bool prepare) {
                                                                                                                      : FF_COLOR_FG_RED),
                         ms);
                 }
-                printf("\e7\e[1A\e[9999999C\e[%dD%s\e8", len - 1, str); // Save; Up 1; Right 9999999; Left <len - 1>; Print <str>; Load
+                if (instance.config.display.pipe) {
+                    // Plain output has no cursor control: the time goes on
+                    // a line of its own after the module's.
+                    printf("%.3fms\n", ms);
+                } else {
+                    printf("\e7\e[1A\e[9999999C\e[%dD%s\e8", len - 1, str); // Save; Up 1; Right 9999999; Left <len - 1>; Print <str>; Load
+                }
             }
         }
 
